<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 150 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 150 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 150 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>The Bank allotted 143 million stg outright in bills maturing on or before July 2 and seven million in repo to July 1 and 2.</p>
<p>Earlier it forecast a money market shortage of 1.15 billion stg and provided 850 million stg in early assistance</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
